Interpretation:
  The low sum is negative in the AP-like rows, but the Paley cut is not the
  damage source there: it is positive in those cases.  The negative mass splits
  between the nonzero-shell mean and the residue-0 trunk.  The
  residue-compressed tournament is small enough to track exactly, while the
  21-channel tournament records whether signs are cyclic/incoherent or nearly
  transitive.  HYP-2867's next proof target is to bound the nonzero mean plus
  residue-0 trunk, using PaleyCut as a balance witness and routing coherent
  sign words to Freiman/GAP atlases.
